ity"}], "description": "Science fiction gives children language for technology, environment, ethics, and social change."}, {"id": "57a786a4-e04a-429b-a6f6-db3c160a5940", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Why Imagination Matters", "children": [{"id": "e7cf87b7-7c97-4e10-bd2a-a474e0a52697", "type": "concept", "title": "symbolism"}, {"id": "fddd76b3-7cf9-44c0-bc0f-6c76258ae99c", "type": "concept", "title": "allegory"}, {"id": "3978dc3c-2b28-4640-8dd1-7b7362b11f9d", "type": "concept", "title": "otherness"}, {"id": "9971f31e-d3b2-48d6-ae85-942023922fca", "type": "concept", "title": "hero's journey"}, {"id": "b55ed5b2-792f-45a8-b51b-805be210015c", "type": "concept", "title": "chosen one trope"}, {"id": "d9954c8a-bf23-4fe3-8822-a899763adfde", "type": "concept", "title": "ethical choice"}, {"id": "27605f14-478d-405a-8a3a-fb4e62ef9d9f", "type": "concept", "title": "wonder"}, {"id": "b71d8b5c-58a9-40d4-873b-34297b690405", "type": "concept", "title": "fear"}, {"id": "ec895179-bb15-4eec-a2fb-15da2074ddb2", "type": "concept", "title": "series reading"}], "description": "Fantasy and science fiction are not escapes from meaning; they often make identity, power, fear, courage, and justice newly visible."}]}, {"id": "5c64fb07-7182-420c-a421-a097c6958730", "type": "topic", "title": "Nonfiction, Informational Texts, STEM Books, and Inquiry", "description": "Expands children's literature beyond fiction by treating nonfiction as crafted, researched, visually designed writing.", "children": [{"id": "1c31c003-ae13-4adb-bb37-7d947dd65464", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nonfiction Forms and Purposes", "children": [{"id": "e78a3388-56a1-4d31-95f2-c60844e34649", "type": "concept", "title": "expository text"}, {"id": "87d87dbe-f8d1-488b-8faf-2620c996be53", "type": "concept", "title": "narrative nonfiction"}, {"id": "6923724c-1813-4cfe-97d4-e1a643e2d8e2", "type": "concept", "title": "survey book"}, {"id": "d1b01d48-b48d-4826-88fc-cb31a95e3cef", "type": "concept", "title": "concept book"}, {"id": "9